The archive layout and config schema that `crates/mlmf-pt2` reads and writes
(the entry names `archive_format`, `archive_version`, `byteorder`,
`.data/version`, `models/`, `data/weights/`, `data/constants/`,
`data/sample_inputs/`; the weights and constants config fields; and the
`ScalarType` and `Layout` codes) were read from PyTorch 2.14.1 at tag `v2.14.1`
(commit `5c4886908584029761b579af026dcfb627c84070`):
`torch/export/pt2_archive/` (`constants.py`, `_package.py`) and
`torch/_export/serde/schema.py` (blob `1715a72511bb2d6140ca2ae3b7972e1d0f6a6ad0`).
PyTorch's `LICENSE` is a BSD-style licence listing several copyright holders
(GitHub's licence API reports NOASSERTION for that reason); the text as the tag
serves it, sha256
`bd018feef8825e88181c84eb7e3aa4eafb8f08a20d9fd6ef948569610c4a3e43`, is
`crates/mlmf-pt2/LICENSE-pytorch.txt`. No PyTorch source is copied: these are
facts about a file format, and the code is original.

`crates/mlmf-pt2/tests/fixtures/torch_export.pt2` is output of running PyTorch
2.14.1 (`crates/mlmf-pt2/tests/make_fixture.py`) on a tiny module with invented
weights; its `models/model.json` is torch's serialization of that program.
`written_by_mlmf.pt2` is written by this crate from the same parts, and was
loaded with `torch.export.load` (`tests/verify_with_torch.py`) to confirm it.
